Enterprise, Inc. provides public safety technology solutions in the United States and internationally. The company operates in two segments, Software and Services, and Connected Devices. The Software and Services segment develops, manufactures, and sells cloud-based software-as-a-service solutions to capture, store, manage, share, and analyze video and other digital evidence. This segment also offers Axon Evidence, Draft One, Axon Records, Axon Standards, Axon Fusus, Axon Assistant, and others. The Connected Devices segment engages in the development, manufacture, and sale of integrated hardware solutions, such as conducted energy devices under the TASER brand, body cameras, fixed and in-car cameras, drone and counter-drone technologies, accessories, extended warranties, and related hardware products, as well as virtual reality training hardware. The company serves first responders across international, federal, state, and local governments, international governmental entities, commercial enterprises, and consumers through direct sales, distribution partners, and third-party resellers. The company was formerly known as TASER International, Inc. and changed its name to Axon Enterprise, Inc. in April 2017. Axon Enterprise, Inc. was incorporated in 1993 and is headquartered in Scottsdale, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Patrick W. Smith | Founder, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $40,001 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $545K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 28%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $15K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $124K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Axon Enterprise, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $25.7B market cap on $2.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +33% over the past three years and +30% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 61% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $75M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.70\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 23% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 621% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":6.213669477952512},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $17.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 54/100): durably derated by the market; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Industrials peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AXON (AXON) Securities Investigation Notice - Levi & Korsinsky","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/axon-axon-securities-investigation-notice---levi--korsinsky-302939122.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794596400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Head to Head Analysis: Axon Enterprise (NASDAQ:AXON) and TAT Technologies (NASDAQ:TATT)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/head-to-head-analysis-axon-enterprise-nasdaqaxon-and-tat-technologies-nasdaqtatt.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794581933.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":